Z||000000||Steve Normington||06-06-2001||12:44 PM||||I just added a aux gage pod to my 85 SE per <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> <BR>and I may have messed it up. When I put on the right turn signal, both turn signal indicators on the panel light solid, but only the right turn signal actually blinks. The left turn signal doesn't light either indicator, but the left signal blinks. The hazard lights light both indicators solid, but both turn signal lights blink. Also, the tach twitches from just off the peg to the peg as the blinkers are going, and the fuel level goes from 1/2 tank to empty as the blinkers are going. If I turn the blinkers off, the fuel level returns to 1/2 tank and the tach quits twitching. I'm pretty sure that the aux gage pod is wired correctly because it indicates 12 volts on the voltmeter with the key on, 0 with key off, and the voltage drops when the lights are turned on. Also, the oil pressure was pegging high with the key on until I hooked up the sending unit and then it reads 0. As part of the job, I switched the 85 MPH gage assembly for a 120 MPH gage assembly. Everything was working correctly before the switch.<P>PS. The engine will turn over on the starter, but I'm not quite done with the injection/ignition, so it won't run.<P>[Edited to fix hyperlink]<p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||1
